==Problem 3==
A Pascal-like triangle has <imath>10</imath> as the top row and <imath>10</imath> followed by <imath>1</imath> as the second row. In each subsequent row the first number is <imath>10</imath>, the last number is <imath>1</imath>, and, as in the standard Pascal's Triangle, each other number in the row is the sum of the two numbers directly above it. The first four rows are shown below:

<imath>
\begin{tabular}{ccccccc}
&&&10&&&\\
&&10&&1&& \\
&10&&11&&1& \\
10&&21&&12&&1 \\
\end{tabular}</imath>

What is the sum of the digits of the sum of the numbers in the <imath>11</imath>th row? 

