<imath>\qquad\bullet</imath> For <imath>n = 1, 2,</imath> or <imath>3,</imath> if it is at <imath>n,</imath> then it moves to <imath>n+1</imath> with probability <imath>\tfrac{1}{4},</imath> it moves to <imath>n-1</imath> with probability <imath>\tfrac{1}{4},</imath> and it disappears with <imath>\qquad\phantom{\bullet}</imath> probability <imath>\tfrac{1}{2}</imath>.

What is the probability that the frog reaches <imath>{4\,?}</imath>

