Figures <imath>0</imath>, <imath>1</imath>, <imath>2</imath>, and <imath>3</imath> consist of <imath>1</imath>, <imath>5</imath>, <imath>13</imath>, and <imath>25</imath> nonoverlapping unit squares, respectively. If the pattern were continued, how many nonoverlapping unit squares would there be in figure 100?

